{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"b5389bf8-32ca-41c4-b8e8-721ed44663e1","status":"SUCCESS","response":"The integration issues have been resolved, and the root causes have been documented in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-KhxhdK/ANSWER.md).\n\n### Summary of Causes \u0026 Fixes\n\n1. **\"Connect Intervals.icu\" Button 401 Unauthorized Failure**\n   - **Cause:** In [`static/app.js`](file:///tmp/h-KhxhdK/static/app.js), the Connect button was an anchor link (`\u003ca href=\"/api/intervals/auth/init\"\u003e`). Clicking it performed a browser document GET navigation that omitted the `Authorization: Bearer \u003ctoken\u003e` stored in `localStorage`, causing [`server.py`](file:///tmp/h-KhxhdK/server.py) to reject the request with HTTP 401.\n   - **Fix:** Handled the Connect click in [`static/app.js`](file:///tmp/h-KhxhdK/static/app.js) using the authenticated `api()` fetch wrapper (with fallback support via cookie and query parameter). Allowed `POST /api/intervals/auth/init` in [`server.py`](file:///tmp/h-KhxhdK/server.py) to return `{ \"url\": \"...\" }` for client redirection.\n\n2. **Intervals.icu HTTP 400 `invalid_request` (\"Duplicate scope\")**\n   - **Cause:** When calendar sync was added, [`config.py`](file:///tmp/h-KhxhdK/config.py) configured `SCOPES` with both `:READ` and `:WRITE` permissions for the same areas (`ACTIVITY:READ,ACTIVITY:WRITE` and `CALENDAR:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE`). Intervals.icu forbids duplicate/redundant scopes because `WRITE` implies `READ`.\n   - **Fix:** Updated `SCOPES` in [`config.py`](file:///tmp/h-KhxhdK/config.py) to `\"ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE\"`.\n\n3. **Athlete Connection Marked \"expired, reconnect\" After 1 Hour**\n   - **Cause:** Intervals.icu access tokens are perpetual and do not return an `expires_in` or `refresh_token`. In [`server.py`](file:///tmp/h-KhxhdK/server.py), `store_connection()` fell back to `DEFAULT_TOKEN_TTL = 3600`, setting an artificial 1-hour expiration. When the background `refresh_tokens()` thread checked tokens nearing expiration (~55 minutes in) and found no `refresh_token`, it marked the connection as `\"expired, reconnect\"` and cleared the token.\n   - **Fix:** In [`server.py`](file:///tmp/h-KhxhdK/server.py), treated tokens without `expires_in` as perpetual (`expires_at = None`), skipped expiring them in `refresh_tokens()`, and added lazy revocation handling to mark connections as reconnect-required only if an API request returns HTTP 401.\n","duration_seconds":584.447662,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":244799,"output_tokens":56169,"thinking_tokens":41412,"cache_read_tokens":2836766,"total_tokens":300968}}}
